{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Energy Conservation in Thermal Continua.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Energy Conservation in Thermal Continua.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"energy conservation in thermal continua energy conservation in thermal continua","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Energy Conservation in Thermal Continua.md","fileName":"Energy Conservation in Thermal Continua.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Energy Conservation in Thermal Continua","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:55\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Thermal Energy Fundamentals]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Thermal Energy Fundamentals","Volumetric Heat Capacity","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Energy Conservation in Thermal Continua.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Energy Conservation in Thermal Continua.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"energy conservation in thermal continua energy conservation in thermal continua","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Energy Conservation in Thermal Continua.md","fileName":"Energy Conservation in Thermal Continua.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Energy Conservation in Thermal Continua","heading":"Energy Conservation in Thermal Continua","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"For any identifiable portion of a continuum, energy entering plus energy generated must equal energy leaving plus energy stored. Applying the balance to progressively smaller elements produces the differential heat equation that relates spatial heat-flux variation to thermal storage and volumetric generation.\n\nThe storage term depends on mass, [[Volumetric Heat Capacity|heat capacity]], and the rate of temperature change. At steady state it vanishes, but internal sources and boundary fluxes must still balance; in a transient, their mismatch changes the local temperature field.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Thermal Energy Fundamentals","Volumetric Heat Capacity","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Energy Conservation in Thermal Continua.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Energy Conservation in Thermal Continua.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"energy conservation in thermal continua energy conservation in thermal continua","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Energy Conservation in Thermal Continua.md","fileName":"Energy Conservation in Thermal Continua.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Energy Conservation in Thermal Continua","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Thermal Energy Fundamentals","Volumetric Heat Capacity","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}